I've reported the following bug to the Nethack Devteam; and Pat
replied that it's fixed now. Maybe the NH variants want to fix
it as well...

  My saddled pet warhorse died in a minetown shop, and picking
  up the saddle (it was not on the "free square") I was not
  charged for it. My knight was neither inside the shop nor in
  line-of-sight of the shopkeeper when the pet died.

For a Vanilla-conforming fix see Pat's details of the fix...

"     I've checked in a fix to require that the hero be within
the same shop at the time of the drop in order for the saddle
to be marked "no charge".  The hero can be in the doorway or
a shop wall location at the time, he/she doesn't have to be all
the way inside where shop goods are kept."


